+// FORGE_SPD_KING_PAWN_CACHE (default 0 = lock code): the pawn-cache entry also keeps, per colour, the king-pawn
+// terms of evaluate_king - shelter, storm and open-king-file terms, the king-pawn distance term, and the
+// `shelter` sum that feeds king danger. They depend only on both sides' pawns and that colour's king square. A
+// record is used only when the stored pawn bitboards and king square equal the position's own (compared
+// directly, not through the pawn key), so every evaluation equals the lock's. The entry becomes one 64-byte
+// cache line. Like the lock's own pawn cache, records assume params::table is not changed between evaluations
+// (the engine never writes it); tools and traced or uncached evaluation never use the cache.
+#ifndef FORGE_SPD_KING_PAWN_CACHE
+#define FORGE_SPD_KING_PAWN_CACHE 0
+#endif
